      "updated_at": "2022-12-13T13:26:35Z",
      "body": "@hellohejinyu Ok, so the problem is related to the native classes that are requesting permissions to load, I think, the instances from the corresponding internal Provider of the system.\r\nFor example, to get the Cookie Manager instance on Android, the internal API is calling:\r\n```java\r\n    /**\r\n     * Gets the singleton CookieManager instance.\r\n     *\r\n     * @return the singleton CookieManager instance\r\n     */\r\n    public static CookieManager getInstance() {\r\n        return WebViewFactory.getProvider().getCookieManager();\r\n    }\r\n```\r\n\r\nDidn't know about that because, well, it's an internal Android API.\r\n\r\nI could implement something like @shirne has already done, but before doing that, I would like to try another way, using a \"lazy\" initialization for the Cookie Manager and the other classes.\r\n\r\nBecause this change could be a breaking change, maybe it could be available only starting from plugin version >= 6.",
      "author_association": "OWNER",
      "pin": null,
      "reactions": {
